{
  "objective": "Determine why, beginning at approximately 2026-05-28T09:15:00+00:00, inventory and catalog read requests began intermittently failing with HTTP 429 responses and establish the full scope of the impact (which endpoints/clients were affected and over what time window)."
}

{
  "capability": "get_incident",
  "arguments": {
    "incident_id": "inc-002"
  },
  "question": "What service, severity, timing, and current state were recorded when incident inc-002 was reported (who/what was tagged as affected and the reported window)?"
}

{
  "capability": "get_correlated_alerts",
  "arguments": {
    "incident_id": "inc-002",
    "start_time": "2026-05-28T08:45:00+00:00",
    "end_time": "2026-05-28T16:00:00+00:00"
  },
  "question": "Which alerts fired around this incident (from 08:45 to 16:00 UTC on 2026-05-28), and what services/signals did they report so I can identify where 429s originated and which components were affected?"
}

{
  "capability": "query_logs",
  "arguments": {
    "service": "inventory-api",
    "start_time": "2026-05-28T09:00:00+00:00",
    "end_time": "2026-05-28T12:00:00+00:00",
    "contains": "429"
  },
  "question": "Which inventory-api log entries between 2026-05-28T09:00 and 2026-05-28T12:00 UTC record HTTP 429 responses, and what do they show about timestamps, endpoints, client identifiers, and any rate-limiter or upstream error messages?"
}

{
  "capability": "get_metrics",
  "arguments": {
    "service": "cosmos-db",
    "metric": "throttle_count",
    "start_time": "2026-05-28T08:00:00+00:00",
    "end_time": "2026-05-28T16:00:00+00:00"
  },
  "question": "What is the time series of throttled requests (throttle_count) for service 'cosmos-db' between 2026-05-28T08:00:00+00:00 and 2026-05-28T16:00:00+00:00?"
}

{
  "capability": "query_logs",
  "arguments": {
    "service": "catalog-api",
    "start_time": "2026-05-28T09:00:00+00:00",
    "end_time": "2026-05-28T15:15:00+00:00",
    "level": "error",
    "contains": "429"
  },
  "question": "Which catalog-api error logs between 2026-05-28T09:00:00+00:00 and 2026-05-28T15:15:00+00:00 mention HTTP 429 or TooManyRequests, and what endpoints/clients and timestamps do they show?"
}

{
  "capability": "get_service_dependencies",
  "arguments": {"service": "cosmos-db", "direction": "downstream"},
  "question": "Which services depend on cosmos-db (i.e., what downstream services/clients would receive 429s from cosmos-db) so I can enumerate all clients potentially affected and where to search logs next?"
}

{
  "capability": "get_deployments",
  "arguments": {
    "services": ["inventory-api", "catalog-api", "checkout-api", "cosmos-db", "api-gateway"],
    "start_time": "2026-05-28T00:00:00+00:00",
    "end_time": "2026-05-28T12:00:00+00:00"
  },
  "question": "What deployments (service, version, and timestamp) were made to inventory-api, catalog-api, checkout-api, cosmos-db, or api-gateway in the window covering the hours before and during the incident (around 2026-05-28T09:15Z)?"
}

{
  "capability": "search_past_incidents",
  "arguments": {
    "query": "Cosmos DB TooManyRequests 429 bulk-import catalog throttling",
    "k": 5
  },
  "question": "Have past incidents shown catalog bulk-imports or similar jobs causing Cosmos DB throttling (429 TooManyRequests) and, if so, which services/endpoints were impacted and how long did those incidents last?"
}

{
  "capability": "",
  "finished_because": "Existing evidence gives a clear, actionable explanation and scope: (1) service logs show 429 TooManyRequests from cosmos-db on inventory-api (09:16:01) and catalog-api (09:16:28) matching the incident start; (2) alerts show inventory-api p95 latency breached at 09:15 and catalog/checkout symptom alerts shortly after; (3) a catalog-api bulk-import deployment occurred at 09:00, providing a plausible RU-consuming change; and (4) the incident record shows the event window and resolution. Together these establish that unbounded bulk import activity against the shared Cosmos DB container caused RU saturation and 429 throttling for inventory and catalog reads (with downstream checkout impact) beginning ~2026-05-28T09:15:00Z and lasting through mitigation. Additional queries would only duplicate already-correlated logs/alerts or background postmortem findings and would not change the conclusion or the scope of affected services and timeframe."
}
